  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far favors multimodal multiprofile PCA + ResNet50 with avgpool and weighted fusion, reaching 0.639 accuracy and 0.620 F1, while multiprofile RNA-only PCA avgpool also substantially outperformed singleprofile RNA-only PCA. The key uncertainty is whether multiprofile aggregation is still necessary when image features are included. config_017 keeps the best-known PCA/ResNet50/weighted-fusion setup but switches to singleprofile, cleanly testing the profile-setting effect. This is a high-value experiment under a limited budget because it can either confirm that multiprofile aggregation is essential or show that a simpler singleprofile multimodal model is nearly as good, helping decide where to invest remaining experiments."
